ily:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The Company&#8217;s liquidity risk for the next 12 months is described in note 2.1. The term of agreements with strategic partners which gave rise the contract liability recorded in the amount of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-937" decimals="-3" name="ifrs-full:ContractLiabilities" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="f-2586">5,486,000</ix:nonFraction>, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-874" decimals="-3" name="ifrs-full:ContractLiabilities" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="f-2587">6,178,000</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-818" decimals="-3" name="ifrs-full:ContractLiabilities" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="0" id="f-2588">10,907,000</ix:nonFraction> as of December 31, 2023, 2022 and 2021, respectively, are described under note 19.</span></div><div style="margin-top:14pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Capital management</span></div><div style="margin-top:5pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The primary objective of the Company&#8217;s capital management is to continue to execute according to its business plans and budgets in order to achieve profitability and positive cash flow, and to maximize shareholder value.</span></div></ix:continuation><div style="height:45pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">F-56</span></div></div></div><div id="i2ae122d8b4184cbfa96cff0e8b6af601_307"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:63pt;width:100%"><div style="text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Tim